## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/de.svg" width="32" alt="Germany" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', position: 'relative', top: '-2px', marginRight: '8px', border: '1px solid #d1d5db', borderRadius: '2px'}} />Germany

Germany pursues historic strategic diversification with Merz's first Gulf partnerships and expanded Indo-Pacific engagement while achieving breakthrough military transformation through permanent Lithuania brigade deployment and BND operational capability expansion. However, domestic legitimacy faces crisis as CDU falls behind AfD in polling amid unprecedented business criticism and deep internal party divisions, while AfD institutionalization confronts corruption scandal ahead of potential absolute power in Saxony-Anhalt. The combination of external strategic assertiveness and internal political fragility creates fundamental tension in Germany's capacity to sustain expanded international commitments.

**Key developments:**

- **Diplomatic:** Merz visited Saudi Arabia, Qatar, and UAE for the first time as Chancellor, meeting Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman and other leaders to establish strategic partnerships despite human rights concerns. The trip explicitly focused on finding new partners in a 'rauer werdende Welt' (roughening world) and moving away from values-based toward interest-based foreign policy. Merz stated Germany no longer puts Gulf states under 'Generalverdacht' (general suspicion).
- **Diplomatic:** Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi called Merz a person with 'widerwärtiger Charakter' (disgusting character) and expressed hope for government change in Berlin, saying Germany has become 'motor of regression' rather than progress. Merz responded coolly, calling it expression of 'great nervousness and uncertainty.' This followed Merz's threats of increased sanctions pressure on Tehran.
- **Diplomatic:** Wadephul traveled through Singapore, New Zealand, Tonga, Australia, and Brunei to strengthen partnerships and counter Chinese influence. Germany formally recognized Pacific island state of Niue and signed raw materials agreements with Australia. Wadephul emphasized importance of diversifying supply chains and strengthening cooperation with 'gleichgesinnten Ländern' (like-minded countries) amid global upheaval.
- **Security:** The Bundeswehr's Lithuania brigade grew from 500 to 1,800 soldiers and officially took command of the multinational battlegroup Lithuania. This marks Germany's first permanent combat brigade stationed abroad since WWII, eventually reaching 4,800 soldiers plus 200 civilians by 2027. The brigade includes the Panzer Battalion 203 and Panzergrenadier Battalion 122 with heavy armor deployed 30km from Belarus border.
- **Security:** Kanzleramt chief Thorsten Frei announced plans for new BND law giving Germany's foreign intelligence service operational capabilities including disrupting drone communications, disabling crypto wallets, and conducting cyber operations. Opposition criticized proposals as potentially unconstitutional 'Tabubruch' (taboo break) regarding separation between police and intelligence services.

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **Federal President Steinmeier attends Winter Olympics in Italy** — Federal President Frank-Walter Steinmeier attended the Winter Olympic Games in Milan-Cortina, visiting the Olympic village, watching German ice hockey women's team defeat Japan, and expressing hopes for medals and peace. He also witnessed American ski racer Lindsey Vonn's crash. *([zeit.de](https://nord24.de/sport/steinmeier-drueckt-deutschem-team-die-daumen-351278.html))*
- **Defense Minister Pistorius modernizes Bundeswehr with innovation center and recruitment drive** — Defense Minister Boris Pistorius opened a new Bundeswehr innovation center in Erding focused on AI, drones, and future military technology. Separately, the military has sent over 40,000 questionnaires to potential recruits as part of the new voluntary military service system, aiming to recruit 20,000 new soldiers by year-end. *([fr.de](https://deutschland.de/de/news/pistorius-eroffnet-innovationszentrum-der-bundeswehr))*
- **Federal President Steinmeier honors train conductor killed on duty and other ceremonial functions** — Federal President Steinmeier expressed condolences to the family of murdered train conductor Serkan C. at a memorial service in Ludwigshafen. He also announced a state funeral for former Bundestag President Rita Süssmuth and awarded the Silver Laurel Leaf to medal winners from international sports competitions. *([zeit.de](https://zeit.de/gesellschaft/zeitgeschehen/2026-02/bahnmitarbeiter-tod-trauerfeier))*
